WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.583
(gentle music)

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.670
- [Narrator] A series of events

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:25.310
called the menstrual cycle

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:27.410
happens about once every month

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:30.780
to prepare a woman's body for pregnancy.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:34.270
Changing levels of natural
chemicals in the bloodstream

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:37.860
called hormones control these events.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:39.870
The reproductive organs affected

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.853
by these hormones include the vagina,

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:49.750
cervix, uterus,

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:57.053
fallopian tubes, and ovaries.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:01.160
The ovaries produce two main hormones

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.743
called estrogen and progesterone.

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:09.110
As the level of estrogen begins to rise,

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.480
it causes the normally thick mucus

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:13.963
inside the cervix to thin out.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.000
Estrogen also triggers other hormones

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.360
to cause one of the
ovaries to release an egg.

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:25.023
This process is called ovulation.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:29.470
If a woman has sex during this time,

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:32.720
a man's reproductive cells, called sperm,

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:36.483
can pass through the thinner
mucus to fertilize an egg.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:42.460
In the uterus, estrogen
causes the lining to thicken,

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:45.583
which prepares it to
receive a fertilized egg.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:50.530
Rising progesterone levels
cause glands in the lining

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:54.053
to release fluid that
feeds the fertilized egg.

00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:58.520
Progesterone also causes
the thinned-out mucus

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:01.120
in the cervix to become thick again,

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.863
which prevents sperm from passing through.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.450
If an egg hasn't been fertilized,

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:12.450
the levels of both estrogen
and progesterone begin to fall.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.900
This drop in hormone
levels causes menstruation,

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.760
a process where the uterus
sheds its inner tissue lining

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.833
and blood through the vagina.

00:02:25.698 --> 00:02:28.510
An intrauterine device, or IUD,

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:31.560
is a birth control method
consisting of a soft,

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.623
flexible T-shaped device with
a thin string on the end.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:40.040
There are two types of
intrauterine devices:

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:44.513
hormonal IUDs and a copper IUD.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:47.260
To prevent pregnancy,

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:51.090
a doctor places an IUD
inside a woman's uterus

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:54.063
with the string hanging
down inside her vagina.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:58.230
Both types of IUD cause mild inflammation

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.683
of the uterine lining,

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.523
which releases immune cells
and chemicals that kill sperm.

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:13.240
Hormonal IUDs also
contain a synthetic type

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:16.343
of progesterone called levonorgestrel.

00:03:17.748 --> 00:03:20.510
Levonorgestrel mainly prevents pregnancy

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.300
by thickening the mucus inside the cervix,

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.283
which prevents sperm
from entering the uterus.

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:31.230
It also prevents the uterine
lining from thickening

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:34.673
so it is less likely to
receive a fertilized egg.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:42.150
About a month after inserting an IUD,

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:44.070
the doctor may schedule an exam

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:46.223
to make sure it is still in place.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.730
The doctor may also teach the woman

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:52.280
how to check her IUD between visits

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:55.313
by feeling for the
string inside the vagina.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.360
Depending on the type,

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:03.250
an IUD can be left in
place for 3 to 10 years.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:07.010
Women can have their doctor
remove an IUD at any time

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:11.183
for any reason, including
the desire to have children.

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:17.870
An intrauterine device, or IUD,

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:21.043
is one of the most effective
methods of birth control.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:27.800
IUDs are over 99% effective
at preventing pregnancy.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:31.120
This means that less
than 1 out of 100 women

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.680
will become pregnant each
year if they use an IUD

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.673
and check it regularly
for correct placement.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:44.530
However, IUDs are only about 97% effective

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:47.073
if not checked for correct placement.

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:56.650
For more information on
any type of birth control,

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:58.173
talk to your doctor.

